# Documentation ownership rule

One kind of truth, one owner. Update only the owner whose durable truth changed. Never copy current status across documents.

| Document | Owns |
|----------|------|
| `README.md` | Entry, setup, how to run |
| `ARCHITECTURE.md` | Durable architecture |
| `docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md` | How the current code works |
| `docs/STATE.md` | Current development state |
| `docs/ROADMAP.md` | Approved future direction |
| `docs/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` | Speculative ideas |
| `docs/WORKFLOW.md` | Development ratchet |
| `docs/work/` | Task-specific execution |
| `docs/DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md` | Concise completion chronology |
| `docs/decisions/` | Why durable choices were made |
| `docs/history/` | Archived planning — never current truth |

When a file moves, repair links broken by that move. Do not reconstruct another document’s facts “for completeness.”
